==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Havsnejonöga.jpg|thumb|A '''lamprey''']]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|laumprei|lang=enm}}, adopted from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|lampreie|lang=fro}} (Modern ''[[lamproie]]''), from {{etyl|ML.|en}} ''[[lampreda]]'', possibly from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|lampetra|lang=la}}, from a combination of {{m|la|lambō||lick}} + {{term|petra||stone|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlæm.pɹi/|/ˈlæm.pɹeɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|lam|prey|lang=en}}
{{rfap|Theosophical phonics classes, mind you|lang=en|variety=Canada}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any long slender [[primitive]] eel-like [[freshwater]] and saltwater [[fish]] of the [[Petromyzontidae]] [[family]], having a [[sucking]] [[mouth]] with [[rasping]] [[teeth]] but no [[jaw]].

====Derived terms====
* [[brook lamprey]]
* [[European river lamprey]]
* [[sea lamprey]]

